#!/bin/sh
# Before each commit: (0) regenerate the COMMITTED pre-warm cache (bundles/cache/)
# from the current sources — so the curated precompiled artifacts stay in step
# with the tree; each is self-validating, so a skipped regen only costs the
# compiler-free fast path, never correctness (tools/internal/prewarm.mjs). (0b) bake the
# homepage's static extraction into index.html (tools/internal/bake-homepage-crawler.mjs) so the
# root page carries its content for crawlers + LLMs; host-client clears it at boot,
# so a stale bake would only ever affect the crawler snapshot, never a live user.
# (0c) bake the cold-stub index.html into every program directory
# (tools/internal/bake-app-stubs.mjs) so …/apps/<name>/ works on a COLD static host —
# shadowed under the dev server, superseded by the SW once installed.
# (0d) stamp the MEASURED flagship figures (apps/homepage/stats.json, fresh from
# prewarm) into every prose citation — README, declare.md, the FAQ — via
# <!--stat:key--> markers (tools/internal/stamp-stats.mjs), so a quoted number can
# never rot against the artifact it describes. Runs BEFORE assemble/bake so the
# doc pipeline consumes the stamped text.
# (1) rebuild any STALE platform bundle — stamp-version calls
# tools/internal/bundle-freshness.mjs first, so a commit cannot ship a bundles artifact older
# than its inputs; (2) stamp the cache-busting BUILD_ID so every deploy carries a
# build id that reflects the current platform (runtime + bundles + web client + SW +
# committed cache + baked index.html). Idempotent: nothing relevant moved → no regen,
# no rebake, no rebuild, no restamp, no churn.
#
# Order matters: prewarm + bake write BEFORE stamp-version hashes bundles/ and
# index.html into the BUILD_ID, so a source change rebumps the id (dropping the SW
# cache bucket on deploy).
#
# Committed + shared (not the per-clone .git/hooks/ copy). `npm install` wires it up via the
# package.json "prepare" script; to activate by hand: git config core.hooksPath tools/hooks
# ONE door. Every committed artifact that is derived from the tree — the prewarm
# cache, the documentation model, the production builds and the stats.json they
# embed, the baked static surfaces, the platform bundles, the build id — is
# regenerated by tools/internal/derive.mjs, which owns the dependency ORDER.
# That door is opened by `npm run derive`, and enforced at pre-push. It is NOT
# opened here: deriving on every commit charges a distro build to an act that is
# not a publication.
#
# That order is not obvious and is why this was a chain of hand-listed commands
# before: prewarm writes apps/homepage/stats.json, and declarec EMBEDS it, so a
# dist built before prewarm is stale the instant prewarm moves a number. Three
# commits in a row on main were that cycle, each one someone reading a test
# failure and running the command it named.
# COMMIT ONLY CHECKS. The full regeneration moved to pre-push (see that hook):
# a commit is a local checkpoint, but the derived artifacts are the DISTRO — this
# repo is what gets served — and a distro only has to be coherent when it is
# PUBLISHED. --check is the manifest's fast path (~0.4s against ~22s for a real
# rebuild when a platform input has moved), and it never blocks: it reports, and
# pre-push is what actually holds the line.
node tools/internal/derive.mjs --dry >/dev/null 2>&1 || {
  echo "note: derived artifacts are stale — 'npm run derive' (pre-push will insist)"
}

# the .declare files THIS COMMIT stages, canonicalized (staged only — formatting
# the whole corpus here would let an unrelated commit silently reformat and stage
# files the author never touched)
DECLARE_FILES=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM -- '*.declare' | grep -v '^docs/system-design/')
[ -n "$DECLARE_FILES" ] && node tools/format.mjs --write $DECLARE_FILES >/dev/null 2>&1
[ -n "$DECLARE_FILES" ] && git add $DECLARE_FILES 2>/dev/null
exit 0
